%% the_meet · 04 · Data Analyst
%% Source of truth: generate.py (CONFIG["analyst"])
%% The `box` matters: AI-DESK is shipped with the client, so the profiling, the
%% SQL and the charts all happen in the analyst's browser. Nothing is sent out to
%% AI-DESK — the only thing outside the box is DATAHUB, touched for a real table.
sequenceDiagram
    box rgb(241, 245, 249) CLIENT — the analyst's browser, where the work happens
    participant C as the analyst · BYOK
    participant A as AI-DESK<br/>shipped with the client
    end
    participant H as DATAHUB<br/>only when a real table is needed

    C->>A: the question, in the tab
    A->>A: 1 reads the file and profiles every column
    A->>A: 2 drafts the SQL and runs it in the browser
    A->>A: 3 renders charts and keeps the follow-ups
    A->>A: rows never leave the tab — the model uses the analyst's own key
    A->>H: only for a real table — catalogue and query execution
    H-->>A: the rows
    A-->>C: the answer, in the same conversation
